                                                               ; What must be clear on entry is what this routine ADDS
                                                               ; into: hashcore's two counts and its prefix buffer; A
                                                               ; blanket claim over the whole frame was wrong and said
                                                               ; so the second time HKDF entered here; hashcore leaves
                                                               ; its digest in H and the last block's schedule in the
                                                               ; window  and is entitled to  because it clears both
                                                               ; itself on the way in;
                                                               ; ASSERT zero 520:971

; ============================================================ ; is the key longer than a block
                                                               ; HMAC replaces a key longer than a hundred and twenty
                                                               ; eight bytes with its hash; the comparison is that
                                                               ; many borrowing decrements of a copy  which is cheaper
                                                               ; to write and to read than a general one;
